/*!
\page page_stetofcollection StETofCollection — Collection Documentation

\section etof_overview Overview

\ref StETofCollection is the event-level container for all data produced by the
<b>Endcap Time-of-Flight (eTOF)</b> detector — an array of Multi-gap Resistive
Plate Chamber (MRPC) modules at forward rapidity extending STAR particle
identification beyond mid-rapidity.

Each event's collection holds:
- \ref StETofDigi — electronic digitisations from individual MRPC strip-ends.
- \ref StETofHit  — reconstructed hits formed from coincident digis on both sides of a counter.
- \ref StETofHeader — event-wise header with trigger timestamps and front-end status.

\ref StETofPidTraits live on the associated track, not in this collection.

\section etof_ownership Object Ownership

- <b>mETofHeader</b> (\ref StETofHeader*): Owned. Assigned via \c setHeader() and
  <b>deleted by the destructor</b>.
- <b>mETofDigis</b> (\c StSPtrVecETofDigi): Owned; \c StSPtrVec deletes elements on destruction.
- <b>mETofHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecETofHit): Owned; same semantics.
- The collection itself is owned by the \c StEvent framework.

\section etof_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \ref StETofHeader* | mETofHeader | Event header: trigger timestamps, bTOF clock reset time, front-end mismatch patterns. Owned and deleted by this class. |
| \c StSPtrVecETofDigi | mETofDigis | Raw digitisations from individual MRPC strip-ends (\ref StETofDigi). |
| \c StSPtrVecETofHit | mETofHits | Reconstructed MRPC hits (\ref StETofHit) formed from ≥2 digis. |

\section etof_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c etofHeader() | Pointer to the eTOF event header (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c etofDigis() | Reference to the digi collection (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c etofHits() | Reference to the reconstructed hit collection (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c setHeader(StETofHeader*) | Assigns the header pointer; collection takes ownership. |
| \c addDigi(const StETofDigi*) | Appends a digi (null-safe). |
| \c addHit(const StETofHit*) | Appends a reconstructed hit (null-safe). |
| \c digisPresent() const | Returns \c true if the digi collection is non-empty. |
| \c hitsPresent() const | Returns \c true if the hit collection is non-empty. |

\section etof_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StETofCollection* etofColl = event->etofCollection();
if (!etofColl) return;

if (etofColl->hitsPresent()) {
    const StSPtrVecETofHit& hits = etofColl->etofHits();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
        StETofHit* hit = hits[i];
        unsigned int sector  = hit->sector();
        unsigned int zPlane  = hit->zPlane();
        unsigned int counter = hit->counter();
        double       time    = hit->time();
    }
}
\endcode

\see StETofHit, StETofDigi, StETofHeader
*/
